From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Velez Garcia <velezgarciaemmanuel25@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:01:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Spread join floods over several ticks

Completing a login reads player data, enters the world, starts entity
tracking and runs every plugin's PlayerJoinEvent. With eighty plugins
loaded that is real work, and a restart or a proxy reconnect delivers all
of it in the same tick - so the first seconds after a restart, exactly
when everyone is trying to get back in, are the seconds the server can
least afford it.

network.maxLoginsPerTick, default 3, caps how many finish per tick. That
is still sixty players a second, so nobody waits noticeably; a login that
does not get through is picked up on the next tick, well inside the 600
tick login timeout. 0 removes the limit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

