+                "\n" +
+                "Completing a login is expensive: player data is read, the world is entered,\n" +
+                "the entity starts being tracked, and every plugin's PlayerJoinEvent runs. On\n" +
+                "a server with eighty plugins that is real work, and a restart or a proxy\n" +
+                "reconnect delivers all of it at once - so the first seconds back up, exactly\n" +
+                "when everyone is trying to reconnect, are the seconds the server can least\n" +
+                "afford it.\n" +
+                "\n" +
+                "At 3 per tick the server still admits sixty players a second, so nobody\n" +
+                "waits noticeably, and the work is spread instead of arriving in one lump.\n" +
+                "0 removes the limit.")
+        public int maxLoginsPerTick = 3;
+    }
